                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 224—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Clipping from the Berliner Correspondenz, March 16,
                        1895</hi>.</head>
                <p>According to the Imperial chancellor’s declaration in the Reichstag on February
                    15 last, the Federal Government, without prejudice to the Imperial currency
                    system, but while recognizing the injurious effect upon industrial enterprise of
                    the increasing difference in value between gold and silver, is about to take
                    into consideration the bringing about of an exchange of views with the
                    governments of other States as to joint remedial measures.</p>
                <p>In consequence of this declaration, of which notice has with satisfaction been
                    taken, the Staatsrath is of opinion that no further measures should be taken at
                    this time, but that the result of the proposed steps should be awaited.</p>
            </div>
